# ORC.ReaperOSC -- REAPER's OSC pattern file for the ORC-1 DAW surface (orc1_dawsurf_bridge.py,
# dialect orc1_dawsurface_osc.py). Built 2026-11-09 from REAPER 7.81's own Default.ReaperOSC
# (/opt/REAPER/Plugins/Default.ReaperOSC on the Pi): same action names and flags, only the
# patterns the ORC uses, so REAPER sends no feedback nobody reads.
#
# INSTALL (on the PC running REAPER):
#   1. Copy this file into REAPER's OSC folder: Options > Preferences > Control/OSC/web >
#      Add > OSC (Open Sound Control) > "Pattern config: (open config directory)", drop the file
#      there, close and reopen the dialog, pick "ORC" in the Pattern config list.
#   2. Mode: "Configure device IP+local port".
#      Device IP   = the Pi (192.168.1.20)      Device port = 9100 (cfg.DAWSURF_OSC_LISTEN_PORT)
#      Local listen port = 8100 (cfg.DAWSURF_OSC_SEND_PORT: the ORC sends here)
#      Leave "Allow binding messages to REAPER actions and FX learn" OFF.
#   3. On the Pi: cfg.DAWSURF_DIALECT = "osc" and cfg.DAWSURF_OSC_HOST = the PC's IP.
#
# ONE DEVICE SEES EVERY TRACK BY NUMBER. DEVICE_TRACK_COUNT is the size of the bank REAPER
# reports, and the bank only moves when the ORC says so (DEVICE_TRACK_BANK_FOLLOWS DEVICE).
# With 512, /track/1 .. /track/512 are REAPER's tracks 1-512 and every view (Fire page, BSP,
# CC strips) is the bridge's own window into them: independent per surface if wanted.
# Past 512 the bridge PAGES: it sends /device/track/bank/select 2 (tracks 513-1024) when a view
# moves there, and the strips mean the next 512. Bigger = more feedback traffic on a refresh
# (about 10 messages per EXISTING track); raise it if you really have more tracks, the bridge
# reads cfg.DAWSURF_OSC_TRACKS and must match this number.

DEVICE_TRACK_COUNT 512
DEVICE_SEND_COUNT 0
DEVICE_RECEIVE_COUNT 0
DEVICE_FX_COUNT 0
DEVICE_FX_PARAM_COUNT 0
DEVICE_FX_INST_PARAM_COUNT 0
DEVICE_MARKER_COUNT 0
DEVICE_REGION_COUNT 0

REAPER_TRACK_FOLLOWS REAPER
DEVICE_TRACK_FOLLOWS DEVICE
DEVICE_TRACK_BANK_FOLLOWS DEVICE
DEVICE_FX_FOLLOWS DEVICE
DEVICE_ROTARY_CENTER 0

# ---- transport (t = toggle / trigger; REAPER answers 1 / 0) ----
RECORD t/record
STOP t/stop
PLAY t/play
PAUSE t/pause
REPEAT t/repeat
REWIND b/rewind
FORWARD b/forward
SCRUB r/scrub

# ---- master ----
MASTER_VOLUME n/master/volume
MASTER_PAN n/master/pan
MASTER_VU n/master/vu

# ---- tracks, by number inside the bank (@ = 1 .. DEVICE_TRACK_COUNT) ----
# TRACK_NUMBER tells which slots hold a track: REAPER fills it for a real track. The bridge
# treats an empty number (and no name) as "no track here" = the end of the list.
TRACK_NAME s/track/@/name
TRACK_NUMBER s/track/@/number/str
TRACK_MUTE b/track/@/mute t/track/@/mute/toggle
TRACK_SOLO b/track/@/solo t/track/@/solo/toggle
TRACK_REC_ARM b/track/@/recarm t/track/@/recarm/toggle
TRACK_SELECT b/track/@/select
# volume twice: n = the fader POSITION as REAPER draws it (its fader-shape preference), and
# f .../db = the level in dB. The bridge learns where 0 dB sits from the pairs REAPER sends and
# sets 0 dB exactly by dB (the Fire's unity column).
TRACK_VOLUME n/track/@/volume
TRACK_VOLUME f/track/@/volume/db
TRACK_VOLUME_TOUCH b/track/@/volume/touch
TRACK_PAN n/track/@/pan
# meters: the busiest feedback. Comment this line out if the network chokes.
TRACK_VU n/track/@/vu

# ---- sent BY the ORC ----
# 41743 = "Control surface: Refresh all surfaces" (REAPER re-sends every pattern above): the
# bridge's hello, repeated until REAPER answers.
ACTION i/action t/action/@
DEVICE_TRACK_COUNT i/device/track/count
DEVICE_TRACK_BANK_SELECT i/device/track/bank/select
DEVICE_TRACK_BANK_FOLLOWS s/device/track/bank/follows
